---
description: "dot: dotcore (public class libs, pycore counterpart) + dotapps (apps). English/ASCII in code."
globs: dotcore/**, dotapps/**
alwaysApply: false
---
# Dot rule (dotcore + dotapps)
- Code/comments/strings: English, ASCII only.
- `dotcore/` = multi-app public libs only (`DotCore.<Name>`, namespace `DotCore.*`); `dotapps/<App>/` = runnable apps (assembly=folder, namespace `DotApps.<App>`). App-specific libs go under their `dotapps/<App>/`, never dotcore. No apps in dotcore, no libs in dotapps.
- Deps flow one way: apps→libs; libs never reference apps and never cycle. Foundations: BCL only; Common: +Foundations; Utils/Infrastructure: +Common; UIInspect: optional 3rd-party.
- App→lib ref: `..\..\dotcore\DotCore.<Name>\*.csproj`; lib→lib: `..\DotCore.<Name>\*.csproj`; tests live in `dotcore/tests/`.
- Register every new project in `dotcore/dotcore.sln`. Build/run via `dotcore/dotcore.sln` or `dotapps/start.ps1`.
